main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ deleted through a call result: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
"delete argument must have offset zero" fails: the address of the most
derived object is attached to a delete-expression only when its operand
has no side effects (typecheck_expr_delete); for `delete make()' the
pointer to the Y subobject reaches __delete.
